   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to permitting membership in certain school related associations by grandparents of certain children",
    "basePrintNo": "A4170",
    "basePrintNoStr": "A4170-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2590-h, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A4170A\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: This bill will allow grandparents who\nhave the written permission of their grandchild's parent or legal guard-\nian to participate in the child's school parent's association or\nparent-teacher association within a community school district in the\nCity of New York.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSubdivision 15 of Section 2590-h of the education law is amended by\nadding a new closing paragraph to read as follows: The chancellor shall\nby rule or regulation provide for the involvement including membership,\nin any parent's association or parent-teacher association established\npursuant to this subdivision, of a grandparent of a child who attends a\nschool within the jurisdiction of the community school district, where\nthe parent or other person having legal custody of such child has indi-\ncated in writing that such grandparent provides direct care and exer-\ncises control over the child on a regular basis.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: Although they are not always designated as legal guardi-\nans, grandparents often take a very active role in the lives of their\ngrandchildren, including having custodial care and direct control over\nthe day-to-day life of their grandchildren.  Thus, these grandparents\noften wish to become involved with the parent, or parent-teacher associ-\nation at their grandchild's school. Under current law, unless these\ngrandparents are the designated legal guardians, they have not had an\nofficial designation under the law allowing them to participate in these\nassociations. This legislation would allow grandparents, when given\nwritten permission from the child's parent or legal guardian, to partic-\nipate in parent associations, as determined by a rule or regulation\nformulated by the Chancellor of the New York City Board of Education.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  S.69/A.1640 of 2003-04.  Referred to Senate\nEducation. S.927/A1714 of 2005-06. S.1309/A.2684 of 2007-08\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately; provided that\nthe amendments to subdivision 15 of section 2590-h of the education law\nmade by section one of this act shall be subject to the expiration and\nreversion of such subdivision pursuant to section 17 of chapter 123 of\nthe laws of 2003, as amended, when upon such date the provisions of\nsection two of this act shall take effect.\n\n",
